## Why This Is Asked
This question assesses your ability to design a compact prefix-search data structure and implement tie-breaking logic using a Trie.

## Key Concepts
- Trie with terminal frequencies stored at each node
- Prefix search via traversal to the prefix end node
- DFS collection of all words in the subtree
- Sorting by frequency (descending), then lexicographic order for ties

## Code Example
```javascript
class TrieNode {
  constructor() {
    this.children = new Map();
    this.freq = 0;
  }
}

class Autocomplete {
  constructor() {
    this.root = new TrieNode();
  }

  addWord(word, freq) {
    let node = this.root;
    for (const char of word) {
      if (!node.children.has(char)) {
        node.children.set(char, new TrieNode());
      }
      node = node.children.get(char);
    }
    node.freq = freq;
  }

  getSuggestions(prefix, limit) {
    if (limit <= 0) return [];

    let node = this.root;
    for (const char of prefix) {
      if (!node.children.has(char)) return [];
      node = node.children.get(char);
    }

    const results = [];
    const dfs = (currentNode, path) => {
      if (currentNode.freq > 0) {
        results.push({ word: path, freq: currentNode.freq });
      }
      for (const [char, childNode] of currentNode.children) {
        dfs(childNode, path + char);
      }
    };

    dfs(node, prefix);

    results.sort((a, b) => {
      if (b.freq !== a.freq) return b.freq - a.freq;
      return a.word.localeCompare(b.word);
    });

    return results.slice(0, limit).map(r => r.word);
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests DP on strings, demonstrating memoization vs tabulation and optimization tricks.

## Key Concepts
- Pattern matching with Trie to prune dictionary checks
- Top-down vs bottom-up DP on string indices
- Handling empty inputs and modulo arithmetic

## Code Example
```javascript
function countWays(s, dict){
  const trie = buildTrie(dict);
  const n = s.length;
  const dp = new Array(n+1).fill(0);
  dp[n] = 1;
  for(let i = n-1; i >= 0; --i){
    let node = trie;
    for(let j = i; j < n; j++){
      const c = s[j];
      if(!node.next[c]) break;
      node = node.next[c];
      if(node.end) dp[i] += dp[j+1];
    }
  }
  return dp[0];
}
function buildTrie(words){
  const root = {next:{}, end:false};
  for(const w of words){
    let node = root;
    for(const ch of w){
      if(!node.next[ch]) node.next[ch] = {next:{}, end:false};
      node = node.next[ch];
    }
    node.end = true;
  }
  return root;
}
```

